  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Binglao. PLO variant. D6 determines hole card count (4/5/6) and High or Hi-Lo 8-or-better per deal. Standard Omaha: must use exactly 2 hole + 3 board. Pot Limit betting. 6-max table. Norwegian championship format.',
    Player: "The die shows 5 — this hand is 5-Card Omaha Hi-Lo! You're dealt: A♠ 2♥ K♦ J♣ 7♠. The flop is 3♦ 5♠ Q♥. You have a strong low draw (A-2) and need a low card on turn/river to qualify. Your high is weak. Pot Limit — control the sizing.",
    objective: 'Win the pot by having the highest hand (or best qualifying low hand in Hi-Lo deals) at showdown, or by forcing all opponents to fold.',
    gameplay: '1. **Format Roll**: Dealer rolls die: 1-2 = 4-card, 3-4 = 5-card, 5-6 = 6-card. High/Low is determined by house rule or second roll. 2. **Betting**: Standard Pot Limit structure. 3. **Hand Construction**: You MUST use exactly two cards from your hand and exactly three cards from the community board to form a five-card hand.',
    keyRules: [
      'Pot Limit: The maximum bet or raise is equal to the current total pot.',
      'Qualifying Low: In Hi-Lo rounds, a low hand must consist of five unpaired cards ranked 8 or lower to be eligible.',
      'Scooping: A player who holds both the best high hand and the best qualifying low hand wins the entire pot.',
    ],
